  },
  "kind" : "article",
  "metadata" : {
    "modules" : [
      {
        "name" : "swift-bundler"
      }
    ],
    "role" : "article",
    "roleHeading" : "Article",
    "title" : "Migrating projects to Swift Bundler"
  },
  "primaryContentSections" : [
    {
      "content" : [
        {
          "anchor" : "Adding-Swift-Bundler-support-to-a-SwiftPM-project",
          "level" : 2,
          "text" : "Adding Swift Bundler support to a SwiftPM project",
          "type" : "heading"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "Swift Bundler is built on top of SwiftPM, so if you have a SwiftPM package then you’re already most of the way to having a Swift Bundler project.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "All you have to do is create a ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "code" : "Bundler.toml",
              "type" : "codeVoice"
            },
            {
              "text" : " file describing the application that you’d like Swift Bundler to build. I’ve included a minimal ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "code" : "Bundler.toml",
              "type" : "codeVoice"
            },
            {
              "text" : " file below.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "code" : [
            "format_version = 2",
            "",
            "[apps.MyApp]",
            "# The product field tells Swift Bundler which SwiftPM executable product to",
            "# build as your app's main executable.",
            "product = \"MyApp\"",
            "identifier = \"com.example.MyApp\"",
            "version = \"0.1.0\""
          ],
          "syntax" : "toml",
          "type" : "codeListing"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "The ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "identifier" : "doc:\/\/swift-bundler\/documentation\/swift-bundler\/configuration",
              "isActive" : true,
              "type" : "reference"
            },
            {
              "text" : " article explains all of the available configuration options in case you’re interested.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "anchor" : "Migrating-from-xcodeproj-to-Swift-Bundler",
          "level" : 2,
          "text" : "Migrating from xcodeproj to Swift Bundler",
          "type" : "heading"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "Swift Bundler has an experimental ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "code" : "convert",
              "type" : "codeVoice"
            },
            {
              "text" : " command that can be used to convert xcodeprojs and xcworkspaces to Swift Bundler projects.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "code" : [
            "swift-bundler convert .\/MyProject.xcodeproj --out .\/MySwiftBundlerProject",
            "cd MySwiftBundlerProject"
          ],
          "syntax" : "sh",
          "type" : "codeListing"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "Please note that the ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "code" : "convert",
              "type" : "codeVoice"
            },
            {
              "text" : " command is very experimental, and its output often requires manual fix ups to get your app compiling as intended, but it should generally provide a good starting point if it manages to parse and understand your project.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "To test out whether your migration has succeeded, try running your app, and loop until you’ve fixed all of the issues.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "code" : [
            "# Run your app (make sure to execute this inside the output directory you gave",
            "# to the convert command)",
            "swift-bundler run"
          ],
          "syntax" : "sh",
          "type" : "codeListing"
        },
        {
          "anchor" : "Migrating-from-arbitrary-build-systems-to-Swift-Bundler",
          "level" : 2,
          "text" : "Migrating from arbitrary build systems to Swift Bundler",
          "type" : "heading"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "If you’re not using Xcode and you’re not using SwiftPM then you’ll be a bit more on your own.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "Our recommended approach is to first convert your project into a SwiftPM package, and then follow the SwiftPM instructions in the section above.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "Alternatively, you can create a new Swift Bundler project with ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "code" : "swift-bundler create MyProject --template SwiftCrossUI",
              "type" : "codeVoice"
            },
            {
              "text" : " and then copy your code across to the new project, but that is perhaps more disruptive if you’re only wanting to try out hot reloading.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "kind" : "content"
    }
  ],
